<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taj al-Din al-Hasani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1885–1943</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taj al-Din al-Hasani (1885–1943) was a Syrian religious scholar and politician, son of a leading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> cleric. He headed the government of the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> under the French mandate in 1928–1931 and 1934–1936, and in 1941 the Free French made him president of Syria, an office he held until his death in January 1943.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taj-al-din-al-hasani.jpg" alt="Taj al-Din al-Hasani" width="144" height="140" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sammy.aw · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Taj_al-Din_al-Hasani_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
